BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Detail: A conversion runs about $200,000 and only makes sense on a proven location, with Lamar's rule that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (a static face already earns $3,000 a month before it earns a screen [Acquisition Insider - 4PyMov-VjoE @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (00:03:02]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (Acquisition Insider runs the math on one two-sided static board on a decent highway: each face rents for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm ($300 to $800 a month, call it $600, which is about $14,000 a year at full occupancy, but 80% occupancy is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (normal, so you actually collect around $11,500 [4PyMov-VjoE @ 00:01:29]. Costs eat roughly 40%: a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (ground lease to the landowner at 15% to 20% of revenue, electricity if the board is lit, insurance, vinyl) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (printing every time the ad changes, and the state permit renewal. That leaves about $7,000 a year of true) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (cash flow, assuming you sell the ads yourself, and single boards trade at eight to ten times cash flow, so a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (fair price runs $55,000 to $70,000 [4PyMov-VjoE @ 00:02:07]. The Wealth Script writes the revenue formula) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (on one line, faces times price per face times how much of the year they are rented, minus land rent, power) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (and upkeep, and on Lamar's 2025 averages an ordinary static sign brings in about $9,000 a year) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm ([lMUn7vCR_iQ @ 00:02:19]. Economics Decoded shows in a worked example why occupancy is the swing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (variable: a face earning $2,000 per sold month makes $24,000 over twelve months but only $18,000 over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (nine, the unsold time can never be resold, and a fixed land payment still comes due [UcnVlSgvKXE @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (00:06:16].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (Digital conversion is where the money concentrates. Old School Financials prices a 14-by-48 static face at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm ($2,000 a month, or $24,000 a year from one tenant, then converts it: the screen rotates advertisers every 6) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (to 8 seconds, eight businesses each buy a $1,000 slot, and the same pole under the same single permit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (throws off $96,000 a year, four times the rent [EFxC43w3Aa8 @ 00:02:51]. The Wealth Script pulls the fleet) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (reality: about 5,500 Lamar screens brought in roughly $632 million, about $115,000 per screen per year) Tj ET
