BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (The first fight is over what an IOS site even is, and the definition dictates what you buy. Ron Rohde, sitting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (with Tyler Cauble, draws the line at 20% or less site coverage by improvements, with outdoor storage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (allowed by right [q7HQGiIiT_8 @ 00:02:49]. Benji Miller of Negresco Property Group runs a looser box: 30%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (coverage or less with by-right zoning is ideal, and past that the rent tips toward a per-building basis, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (32.5% coverage and demolishable sheds being a different game [7qT_5Pw0cTo @ 00:28:35]. When a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (Chicago residential investor pitched IOS as 3 to 10 acre urban parcels near highways with outdoor-storage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (zoning, Ron pushed back, saying size and infill don't belong in the definition and that it falls apart above 20) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (to 30% building coverage [tonuCLfZrYE @ 00:02:19]. The sharper split is building versus bare dirt. Ron told) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (Jonathan Hayek flatly that a pure yard is off the menu in 2024, because a site without a building gets fewer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (accessory uses by right [mPrS0VognEo @ 00:08:57]. Benji lands in the same place from the leasing side:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (bare paved yards only make sense for drayage or trucking near the port, and sites with buildings lease) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (better. The pure-yard operator lives or dies on port-adjacent drayage demand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (Surface and gate spend split the operators into two camps. The Truck N' Hustle operator, running roughly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (100 spots in Massachusetts at about $500 per spot per month, puts pavement at the top of the build list:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (number one is you want pavement, not crush gravel, followed by striping, numbered spots, around 33) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (perimeter light poles and CCTV that is actually monitored [uZVNo7EIaXA @ 00:01:43]. Ron Rohde runs the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (opposite playbook in DFW. Ron's pick is Class B: gravel, full fencing, a gate and lighting with no frills, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (Ron calls recession-resilient because $400 paved-lot parkers trade down when the market tightens) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm ([tonuCLfZrYE @ 00:19:05]. On gates, Ron still tells builders to install an automatic gate even at Class B,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (because manual gates get left open, and prices a 30 ft cantilever gate with install at about $30K) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm ([rPXHwXgqWs8 @ 00:06:59]. Jose at Rig Hut takes the staged route: test the market under a lease with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (manual gates before investing in automation, then move to an automatic system once you want 24/7) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (access, multiple tenants and expansion beyond one location [Fc82YDH9IrI @ 00:06:10]. Jose concedes that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (five-acre gravel lots in tight markets get away with padlocks purely because demand is high.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (Tenant concentration and rental term are the third fault line. Ron Rohde argues single tenant is a benefit:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (underwrite heavily and bet once, because in a building of 20 to 30 flex tenants at least 5 are financially) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (shaky [-g_D6hbOPNE @ 00:02:17]. Ron frames the choice as a temperament call: with sweat equity,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (choose multi-tenant; if time-constrained, choose single tenant. The Truck N' Hustle operator leans on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (opposite logic and treats many tenants as a shield: with 50 tenants, losing 2 doesn't hurt, though they) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (concede a single tenant is simpler to run and eventually leased the first lot to one tenant [uZVNo7EIaXA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (00:04:16]. On term, Ron's math favors transient parking: $30 a night is about $900 a month per space) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (against $225 to $300 from a monthly tenant, and even at 80% occupancy a daily space yields about $630,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (but it demands heavy marketing through Facebook, trucker apps, forums and signage [tonuCLfZrYE @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (00:10:32]. Rig Hut, having handled about 1,000 vehicles a month at peak around a South Florida port city,) Tj ET
